# JD's content goals

- JD posts **lesson clips only** (real teaching moments), for good. No perfect-loop videos, no trend/fluff, no old-style "Disneyland" looks.
- Goal is the **right students**, not fame. He wants to **stay small** (more students than he can teach = hiring people, which he does not want). He does not want to be SNS famous.
- When reading stats: do NOT judge by raw views alone or push growth tactics. Look for what attracts good-fit students - saves, shares, comments, watch time, "warning" style teaching clips, subscribers/trial-lesson bookings.
- "Warning" clips (don't say X) perform fine and are wanted. Don't call them weak.
- (Oct 9, 2026) JD thinks people are finding him now. He's going to ask new students how they found him and will tell me; until then, don't guess which channel or clip is driving it.
- (Oct 9, 2026) X/Twitter: NOT doing anything on X for now. Later it may be used only to point people to the future free Homework Hub app (text lesson-note posts possible). X creator payouts are not a goal. Don't add X copy to clip posts until JD says.
- Don't suggest loops, hooks-for-reach, posting more often to grow, or going viral.
